{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "003S", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{A} \\to \\mathcal{B} \\to \\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{A}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{B}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{B}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{A}$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{C}$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-fibred-in-groupoids-over-fibred-in-groupoids}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:8a0448bf80414f9b689b867c54c2ee3fe115c3437afa1c0dfbed3541b792a7df", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:94069e3be933a96d49baf5353ff358f46c01c08e695b62a80162b3ebfb143723", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be functors between\ncategories. If <MATH_0002> is fibred in groupoids over <MATH_0003>\nand <MATH_0004> is fibred in groupoids over <MATH_0005>, then\n<MATH_0006> is fibred in groupoids over <MATH_0007>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:95b1cafeb5075d6d7f2c8abd62766bf6f263a04c6ea186dd41ee8cd3c3e94e1d", "unit_id": "tag:09WW:statement"}
{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "003S", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{A}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{A}_U$", "MATH_0004": "$U$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0006": "$x \\to y$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{A}_U$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{B}$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{B}_U$", "MATH_0010": "$x \\to y$", "MATH_0011": "$\\mathcal{A}$", "MATH_0012": "$\\mathcal{B}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-fibred-groupoids}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-fibred-over-fibred}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-composition-cartesian}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{lemma-fibred-groupoids}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:c7b703c6b42877232b38dc31bfa09d474a125a261c8fbde9498571190f5392c1", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c1e549fb2c05db572ebde3051bba0ae5b86f970f8601d03d7c29c7995d9b7810", "source_text": "One can prove this directly from the definition. However, we will argue\nusing the criterion of Lemma <REF_0001>.\nBy Lemma <REF_0002> we see that <MATH_0001>\nis fibred over <MATH_0002>. To finish the proof we show that the fibre\ncategory <MATH_0003> is a groupoid for <MATH_0004> in <MATH_0005>.\nNamely, if <MATH_0006> is a morphism of <MATH_0007>, then its\nimage in <MATH_0008> is an isomorphism as <MATH_0009> is\na groupoid. But then <MATH_0010> is an isomorphism, for example by\nLemma <REF_0003> and the fact that every\nmorphism of <MATH_0011> is strongly <MATH_0012>-cartesian\n(see Lemma <REF_0004>).\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:e6f201310bbb2bac672588c04e89000d76288f72484c625d7eb92f77cb0626bf", "unit_id": "tag:09WW:proof"}
